WEBVTT

00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:04.850
January 8th 02:49 Blue World Fortress No. 4

00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:09.590
Release.

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:13.780
Sword Sniper  Rigel

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:20.410
Original XIII  Type II

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:29.940
You awoke, Type II?

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:35.640
Yes, thanks to a certain 
poorly-made someone, II-3.

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:38.760
Is that a reference to me?

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:41.230
I couldn't say.

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:46.840
Did you forget that we're 
born of the same DNA?

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:52.110
Denying me means denying yourself.

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:55.450
That's very conceited of you, II-3,

00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:57.620
for no more than a degenerate copy.

00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:02.580
Azumi Kagamihara, was it? Your partner.

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:05.500
It seems she's been a bad influence on you.

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:07.610
Azumi has nothing to do with this!

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:11.810
You lose control of your emotions 
over such cheap provocation.

00:01:11.810 --> 00:01:13.580
That's why you're a degenerate copy.

00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:19.530
You'll need to be reformatted 
in the near future.

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:23.140
When that's done, let's meet again.

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:05.080
January 8th 02:59

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:08.040
January 8th 02:59
Blue World Fortress No. 4 - Polaris's Private Room

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:22.520
This is...

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:26.180
An observation report on Azumi Kagamihara?

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:28.290
No, this can't be...

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:30.430
No, it's true.

00:03:32.210 --> 00:03:34.320
Azumi Kagamihara's disease

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:38.860
was artificially induced by 
our injection of nanomachines.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:38.860
Administrator  Polaris

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:41.020
Why would you do that?

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:44.110
To keep her dependent on us.

00:03:44.690 --> 00:03:48.370
The special enzymes in this 
drug can increase or decrease

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:52.020
the amount of poison the nanomachines emit.

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:53.630
In other words,

00:03:54.410 --> 00:03:58.130
this is a chain that binds Azumi Kagamihara.

00:03:58.910 --> 00:04:00.760
Why would you go that far to keep Azumi?

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:06.010
Because she is crucial to 
the future that we seek.

00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:07.760
What does that mean?

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:10.350
City Guard  Phecda

00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:10.830
Rigel.

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:15.570
You've come into contact with 
information you were never to know.

00:04:15.570 --> 00:04:17.470
You will be reformatted,

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:21.280
and all your memories concerning 
Azumi Kagamihara will be deleted.

00:04:22.060 --> 00:04:24.430
I'll forget about Azumi?

00:04:25.230 --> 00:04:28.120
About everything that's happened?

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:39.040
I'll never... I'll absolutely never...

00:04:40.370 --> 00:04:41.550
allow that!

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:46.510
After her!

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:47.370
Yes, ma'am!

00:04:53.510 --> 00:04:56.940
<i>Take care of Azumi, Rigel.</i>

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:13.540
 January 8th 05:11 Eken Temple Graveyard

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:20.730
Did I lose them?

00:05:32.860 --> 00:05:34.310
Type II...

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:36.750
Permission!

00:06:07.570 --> 00:06:09.480
A mere degenerate copy...

00:06:11.450 --> 00:06:16.580
Such a failure isn't like you, 
Administrator Polaris.

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:14.890
January 8th 08:40

00:06:14.890 --> 00:06:18.390
January 8th 08:40
Blue World Fortress No. 4 - Command Room

00:06:16.580 --> 00:06:19.270
I'm terribly sorry.

00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:23.270
We must not allow her to be 
captured by another world.

00:06:23.860 --> 00:06:27.280
Administrator  Vega

00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:28.570
Bring Azumi Kagamihara back, 
whatever it takes, Type II.

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:32.480
Type II?

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:34.410
Administrator Vega...

00:06:35.180 --> 00:06:37.790
Who is Azumi Kagamihara, exactly?

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:42.790
Why are you so attached to a mere human?

00:06:42.790 --> 00:06:43.790
Silence.

00:06:45.110 --> 00:06:49.940
Even if you are an original, there 
are things you should not know.

00:06:49.940 --> 00:06:52.550
You need only follow your orders.

00:06:53.750 --> 00:06:56.060
Yes, my mother.

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:04.060
January 8th 16:44 Cafe Broccolo

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:09.150
Asuka Tennoji                        The Proud  Fierte

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:08.990
No luck again today...

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:13.570
Mikado Kurosaki

00:07:16.270 --> 00:07:19.290
Audium is a special Z/X 
that doesn't need to be

00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:20.580
supplied with resources.

00:07:20.950 --> 00:07:24.210
That's the only conclusion 
we can draw after detecting

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:26.090
no resources after a week's searching.

00:07:26.420 --> 00:07:30.590
Maybe so, but why does that mean 
you have to destroy Kobe?

00:07:30.590 --> 00:07:35.600
You said you felt strong hatred 
towards Z/X from Audium, right?

00:07:36.450 --> 00:07:37.350
Yes.

00:07:37.350 --> 00:07:42.480
Try to recall the first time she appeared.

00:07:47.590 --> 00:07:51.920
When Audium saw Alexander, 
a Z/X of immense power,

00:07:51.920 --> 00:07:54.810
she allowed her hatred to explode.

00:07:54.810 --> 00:07:56.620
Don't you think that's a possibility?

00:07:56.620 --> 00:07:58.120
But still...

00:07:58.120 --> 00:08:03.120
If we have Alexander destroy a large 
area to demonstrate his power,

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:07.130
Audium should appear again, 
driven by her hatred.

00:08:07.130 --> 00:08:08.880
Chitose Aoba

00:08:07.130 --> 00:08:08.880
That's insane, Mikado.

00:08:09.410 --> 00:08:12.290
I'll have the citizens evacuated first.

00:08:12.290 --> 00:08:13.880
No one will be hurt.

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:15.390
That's not the issue!

00:08:16.050 --> 00:08:18.260
I'll give you three days, no more.

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:21.140
Nine Worthies  Alexander

00:08:27.570 --> 00:08:29.020
What do we do?

00:08:29.020 --> 00:08:31.030
Katana Samurai  Rindo

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:34.030
Azumi Kagamihara

00:08:38.990 --> 00:08:40.030
Rigel!

00:08:43.220 --> 00:08:44.040
No way!

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:46.620
Then Azumi's illness...

00:08:46.620 --> 00:08:51.350
Yes. It was all a plot of our world.

00:08:51.350 --> 00:08:52.370
Rigel!

00:08:52.370 --> 00:08:54.310
Don't talk anymore.

00:08:54.310 --> 00:08:55.550
It'll aggravate your wounds.

00:08:58.550 --> 00:09:00.100
Azumi!

00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:02.090
Oh, no! Another attack!

00:09:02.090 --> 00:09:03.100
Not now!

00:09:03.530 --> 00:09:04.590
Do you have her medicine?

00:09:04.590 --> 00:09:06.230
Not anymore.

00:09:06.230 --> 00:09:07.540
No...

00:09:15.490 --> 00:09:18.950
Then take this secret medicine 
handed down within my clan.

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:22.190
That won't work against nanomachines!

00:09:22.190 --> 00:09:23.670
Don't move!

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:27.700
This will be bitter.

00:09:27.700 --> 00:09:28.960
Okay.

00:09:36.500 --> 00:09:38.320
I feel a bit better.

00:09:38.320 --> 00:09:39.930
I'm sure.

00:09:40.360 --> 00:09:43.000
Now just lie down and rest.

00:09:44.220 --> 00:09:46.530
It... worked?

00:09:46.530 --> 00:09:50.230
It cleared out the poison 
from the nanomachines?

00:09:50.740 --> 00:09:56.550
Then, Rindo, couldn't the medicine 
of your world heal her?

00:09:56.550 --> 00:09:59.370
I don't have the knowledge to say,

00:10:00.240 --> 00:10:04.400
but the Eight Great Dragon 
Kings may know a way.

00:10:04.400 --> 00:10:06.130
The Eight Great Dragon Kings?

00:10:08.050 --> 00:10:13.270
The clan that worships the divine 
tree in our world, the Mougi.

00:10:14.250 --> 00:10:18.610
So they could make Azumi well again, right?

00:10:18.610 --> 00:10:20.930
I can't say for sure.

00:10:20.930 --> 00:10:23.010
But there's a possibility, right?

00:10:23.330 --> 00:10:25.310
I think there is.

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:29.430
She's here.

00:10:32.020 --> 00:10:33.230
Type II.

00:10:38.520 --> 00:10:40.030
Is something wrong?

00:10:40.030 --> 00:10:41.350
That's enough.

00:10:41.350 --> 00:10:42.840
But you're still...

00:10:43.730 --> 00:10:44.530
Rigel!

00:10:47.220 --> 00:10:48.540
Azumi...

00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:53.980
Because I met you, 
my own kind is after me,

00:10:53.980 --> 00:10:57.550
and I can no longer return to my 
home as long as I stay with you.

00:10:57.550 --> 00:11:00.550
Rigel, what are you saying?

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:04.120
I'm going back to my world.

00:11:04.790 --> 00:11:06.850
Goodbye, Azumi.

00:11:08.170 --> 00:11:09.140
Wait, Rigel!

00:11:14.640 --> 00:11:15.570
Azumi!

00:11:15.570 --> 00:11:19.070
You're going to leave your partner like this?

00:11:21.310 --> 00:11:24.840
Azumi and I aren't partners anymore.

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:28.120
Rigel...

00:11:30.290 --> 00:11:32.080
Azumi! Azumi!

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:35.130
Hang in there, Azumi! Azumi!

00:11:44.480 --> 00:11:48.240
Azumi Kagamihara isn't 
with you, is she, II-3?

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:50.890
January 8th 19:06 Kobe Eastern Mountains

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:50.310
I left that little jinx behind.

00:11:50.890 --> 00:11:52.140
You're a poor liar.

00:11:52.490 --> 00:11:58.560
The chips installed in our bodies 
allow us to be tracked at all times.

00:11:58.560 --> 00:12:01.010
That's why you parted ways with her, right?

00:12:01.010 --> 00:12:05.870
I suppose you mean to let her escape 
while you're buying time here.

00:12:06.340 --> 00:12:11.160
But I don't think you'll be 
able to buy much time at all.

00:12:12.410 --> 00:12:17.210
Without a partner, you can't receive resources.

00:12:17.210 --> 00:12:19.420
In other words, you can't fight that long,

00:12:19.770 --> 00:12:22.050
and you'll never be able to beat me.

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:23.240
Permission.

00:12:24.780 --> 00:12:27.680
<i>She's right. It'll be hard to beat her.</i>

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:33.850
<i>But if I'm willing to fight to my death, 
I can take her with me!</i>

00:12:34.550 --> 00:12:35.930
Permission!

00:12:51.660 --> 00:12:53.510
Are you okay, Azumi?

00:12:54.520 --> 00:12:57.200
Rigel is fighting.

00:12:58.090 --> 00:12:59.020
Please!

00:12:59.020 --> 00:13:01.140
Take me to Rigel!

00:13:01.140 --> 00:13:03.520
Even if you go now, 
what do you expect to do?

00:13:03.520 --> 00:13:04.970
She left you!

00:13:05.480 --> 00:13:10.740
I know that, but Rigel 
is very important to me.

00:13:11.430 --> 00:13:15.030
If she's fighting, I want to be near her.

00:13:22.660 --> 00:13:24.150
Azumi...

00:13:24.490 --> 00:13:26.770
Asuka? You...

00:13:26.770 --> 00:13:28.990
Let's go, Azumi.

00:13:29.330 --> 00:13:33.200
January 8th 19:17 Kobe Fountain Park

00:13:30.660 --> 00:13:32.140
Are you cold?

00:13:32.140 --> 00:13:33.620
I'm okay.

00:13:37.880 --> 00:13:39.390
Oww!

00:13:39.880 --> 00:13:41.590
What are you guys doing?

00:13:43.240 --> 00:13:44.710
We're going, too!

00:13:44.710 --> 00:13:46.840
I can't trust you on your own.

00:13:46.840 --> 00:13:49.300
Hurry or we'll leave you behind.

00:13:49.300 --> 00:13:51.810
H-Hey, hang on!

00:13:55.340 --> 00:13:56.580
Those guys...

00:13:57.580 --> 00:13:59.090
They're not so bad.

00:13:59.100 --> 00:14:00.940
We're going, too.

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:03.740
Again?!

00:14:03.740 --> 00:14:04.520
Let's go.

00:14:04.520 --> 00:14:10.810
I told you, Fierte, I don't like heights!

00:14:12.620 --> 00:14:15.910
January 8th 19:21 Kobe Sea Hotel

00:14:15.910 --> 00:14:18.160
Sera, you'll catch cold.

00:14:18.160 --> 00:14:20.170
If you want to sleep, go to your room.

00:14:20.750 --> 00:14:24.380
Sera Kurashiki

00:14:22.770 --> 00:14:25.670
What? You haven't eaten dinner yet?

00:14:26.020 --> 00:14:29.430
No. I'll eat when I'm done 
looking at these documents.

00:14:29.430 --> 00:14:32.200
You won't grow up big and strong that way.

00:14:32.640 --> 00:14:35.600
January 8th 19:31 Kobe Eastern Mountains

00:14:56.960 --> 00:14:58.100
Release.

00:14:59.540 --> 00:15:02.790
Feeling low on power without your resources?

00:15:05.800 --> 00:15:08.500
Let's play some more, II-3.

00:15:19.470 --> 00:15:20.730
What's that?

00:15:21.510 --> 00:15:22.480
Rigel!

00:15:36.880 --> 00:15:38.990
I pity you, II-3.

00:15:38.990 --> 00:15:42.250
This is what you get for siding with humans.

00:15:51.050 --> 00:15:54.980
It'd be easy to kill you, but my 
orders were to bring you back.

00:15:55.420 --> 00:15:56.760
This is Type II.

00:15:57.090 --> 00:16:00.770
Administrator Vega, I've secured II-3.

00:16:00.770 --> 00:16:02.700
Requesting permission to transfer.

00:16:03.450 --> 00:16:05.610
Understood. Permission granted.

00:16:08.760 --> 00:16:11.020
<i>I'm sorry, Azumi.</i>

00:16:11.700 --> 00:16:13.930
<i>I... I...</i>

00:16:14.440 --> 00:16:17.780
<i>I'm going to forget you!</i>

00:16:25.030 --> 00:16:26.540
Resources?

00:16:36.430 --> 00:16:39.810
So Azumi Kagamihara is nearby?

00:16:39.810 --> 00:16:42.680
Azumi is not the only one nearby!

00:16:45.460 --> 00:16:46.550
Rindo!

00:16:46.550 --> 00:16:47.440
Fierte!

00:16:51.070 --> 00:16:55.320
I've nothing against you, 
but honor compels me to fight!

00:17:14.550 --> 00:17:15.570
Azumi?

00:17:18.660 --> 00:17:20.860
I'm sorry, Rigel.

00:17:21.640 --> 00:17:23.280
Why are you apologizing?

00:17:23.280 --> 00:17:26.890
It's my fault this happened to you.

00:17:26.890 --> 00:17:30.270
No, it's not your fault.

00:17:30.270 --> 00:17:33.190
I did all this because I wanted to.

00:17:33.190 --> 00:17:36.600
You're a precious friend to me.

00:17:36.600 --> 00:17:37.700
Rigel...

00:17:38.380 --> 00:17:41.740
I'm the one who needs to apologize.

00:17:42.580 --> 00:17:46.080
I'm sorry I said such awful things.

00:17:47.780 --> 00:17:49.350
That's not true...

00:17:49.810 --> 00:17:51.550
That's not true.

00:17:52.040 --> 00:17:56.070
It's true that you lost your home.

00:17:57.090 --> 00:17:58.120
No.

00:17:58.620 --> 00:18:00.350
I have a home.

00:18:01.600 --> 00:18:06.010
The resources you gave me were so warm.

00:18:06.010 --> 00:18:08.750
Warmer than anything I've ever felt.

00:18:09.680 --> 00:18:13.390
My home is with you.

00:18:13.890 --> 00:18:17.820
So I won't say goodbye again.

00:18:18.880 --> 00:18:21.620
I'll be back soon, Azumi.

00:18:26.010 --> 00:18:27.290
Permission!

00:18:33.940 --> 00:18:35.330
See you soon,

00:18:39.030 --> 00:18:40.100
Rigel!

00:18:44.520 --> 00:18:45.060
What?

00:18:51.190 --> 00:18:52.840
What is this power?

00:18:52.840 --> 00:18:56.500
Is this the power of one who 
has something to protect?

00:18:56.500 --> 00:18:57.930
That's right, Type II.

00:18:57.930 --> 00:18:59.920
I'm sure you wouldn't understand.

00:18:59.920 --> 00:19:03.260
I never would have if I hadn't met Azumi!

00:19:03.260 --> 00:19:05.950
Having someone to protect makes you strong!

00:19:07.320 --> 00:19:07.950
Azumi!

00:19:09.430 --> 00:19:11.460
Resource reboot!

00:19:19.080 --> 00:19:21.660
What power.

00:19:22.980 --> 00:19:28.730
I can't believe a copy is succeeding 
so well against the original.

00:19:29.060 --> 00:19:29.980
January 8th 20:22

00:19:29.070 --> 00:19:33.480
It just shows that even we 
can't predict everything.

00:19:29.980 --> 00:19:32.940
January 8th 20:22
Blue World Fortress No. 4 - Command Room

00:19:35.410 --> 00:19:40.740
<i>Of course, even I didn't 
expect her to go this far.</i>

00:19:41.490 --> 00:19:46.240
<i>I suppose true strength is only 
found within the human heart.</i>

00:19:47.400 --> 00:19:51.250
<i>You're human, without a doubt, Rigel.</i>

00:19:51.540 --> 00:19:54.960
January 8th 20:25 Kobe Eastern Mountains

00:19:53.750 --> 00:19:55.190
No way!

00:19:55.190 --> 00:19:56.250
There're so many!

00:20:03.990 --> 00:20:04.760
Azumi!

00:20:05.420 --> 00:20:06.440
I'm okay.

00:20:06.440 --> 00:20:07.720
You're not okay!

00:20:07.720 --> 00:20:10.320
You can't supply resources in your condition.

00:20:10.320 --> 00:20:11.770
Resources...

00:20:11.770 --> 00:20:14.020
That's it! Resources!

00:20:14.020 --> 00:20:14.870
What?

00:20:14.870 --> 00:20:16.020
She's a Z/X, too.

00:20:16.020 --> 00:20:18.030
She has to have a partner somewhere.

00:20:18.030 --> 00:20:19.490
If we can find them...

00:20:19.490 --> 00:20:20.790
That's right!

00:20:27.530 --> 00:20:28.480
Did you find them yet?

00:20:28.480 --> 00:20:30.160
Hang on! It's not that simple!

00:20:32.540 --> 00:20:33.710
I found them!

00:20:33.710 --> 00:20:34.540
All right!

00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:39.340
January 8th 20:32 Kobe - Ikemizu Tower

00:20:39.920 --> 00:20:41.380
Rigel, can you hear me?

00:20:41.380 --> 00:20:42.920
Bearing 2-3-0.

00:20:43.840 --> 00:20:45.060
Go, now!

00:20:45.060 --> 00:20:46.030
Thanks!

00:20:46.030 --> 00:20:46.930
Permission!

00:20:49.570 --> 00:20:51.810
Angle of inclination: +2 degrees.

00:20:51.810 --> 00:20:53.310
Rigel, fire!

00:20:53.630 --> 00:20:54.890
Shoot!

00:21:08.750 --> 00:21:12.950
I-Impossible. They located my device?

00:21:13.720 --> 00:21:16.460
You lose, Type II.

00:21:16.960 --> 00:21:20.660
Go home and tell Vega and the others: 
I won't let them have Azumi.

00:21:20.660 --> 00:21:23.210
I'll protect her, no matter what.

00:21:23.830 --> 00:21:25.470
You'll regret this.

00:21:33.270 --> 00:21:33.980
That's...

00:21:41.040 --> 00:21:42.360
Audium!

00:21:42.650 --> 00:21:46.320
January 8th 20:45 Kobe Sea Hotel

00:21:42.850 --> 00:21:44.020
Mikado!

00:21:44.020 --> 00:21:45.530
Okay, I'm going!

00:21:45.530 --> 00:21:47.960
Wait! We need more information!

00:21:50.240 --> 00:21:52.240
Hi-yah!

00:21:53.220 --> 00:21:54.720
Just has to have his way...

00:21:55.520 --> 00:21:57.170
What's going on?

00:21:57.170 --> 00:21:58.250
It's Audium.

00:21:59.490 --> 00:22:00.970
Audium?

00:22:00.970 --> 00:22:02.250
